1
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,000
[Gon] Ging is spelled G-I-N-G.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,000
[Bisky] Oh, I see!

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
So "Nigg" is an anagram.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
[Gon] My guess is that
when I was just a baby,

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
I must have come here with Ging.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Maybe this was his way
of trying to tell me…

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
if I'm ready to give up everything I have

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,000
and go find him,

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:33,000
then I have to get strong enough
to clear the game.

10
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Well, what are you planning to do
once you find Ging?

11
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:38,000
That's easy.

12
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,000
-I'll introduce him to Killua.
-Huh?

13
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
I'll tell him he's
my best friend in the world!

14
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Accompany on!

15
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Nigg!

16
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,000
[opening theme music playing]

17
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

18
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,000
[singer singing in English]

19
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

20
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,000
[singer singing in English]

21
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:38,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

22
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,000
[singer singing in English]

23
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

24
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,000
REUNION X AND X UNDERSTANDING

25
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,000
[Gon gasps]

26
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,000
[Killua] Wait. Is that Gon's…

27
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,000
G-Ging.

28
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
-[ground crunches]
-[gasps]

29
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,000
[both grunt]

30
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
In my mouth is a roulette

31
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
containing the numbers one
all the way through nine.

32
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
You get a different weapon
for each number on the wheel.

33
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,000
I am the great mad clown, Crazy Slots!

34
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Hope you get something good!
[babbles]

35
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Four!

36
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
[man] Damn, bad roll.

37
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:46,000
[Crazy Slots] Shut up!
Be grateful, you idiot!

38
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:49,000
[gunshots]

39
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,000
[Killua] What the…

40
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,000
an ant?

41
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,000
-[man] Are you hurt?
-[both gasp]

42
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,000
[gun clicks]

43
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:15,000
[Killua] Is it him? Is that Ging?

44
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
[gasps]

45
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,000
-This isn't Ging.
-What?

46
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Hang on.

47
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,000
What was that all about? Tell us!

48
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,000
First you knock us down.

49
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Then you start firing at us!

50
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Stop messing around!

51
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,000
[man] "Messing around"?

52
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Quite the opposite.

53
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,000
If I hadn't opened fire,

54
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,000
you both would have been attacked.

55
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,000
[Killua] Yeah, by what,

56
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,000
that stupid ant you shot?

57
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,000
[growls]

58
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,000
[yells]

59
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
What is this?

60
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,000
[man] You fool!

61
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,000
[Gon gasps]

62
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,000
That was no ordinary ant.

63
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,000
It's a Chimera Ant.

64
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,000
[Killua] A what?

65
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,000
[man] An aggressive, carnivorous insect

66
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,000
that's been designated
quarantine level one.

67
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:29,000
They even attack humans
from time to time.

68
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,000
[Killua gasps]

69
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
You boys didn't realize it,

70
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
but you were standing
right in front of their nest.

71
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:38,000
If I hadn't fired the moment I did,
an army of Chimera Ants

72
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,000
would have consumed
the both of you by now.

73
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,000
[Gon gasps]

74
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:48,000
I feel like this has happened before.

75
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,000
[man sighs]

76
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:58,000
Don't worry. It's not serious.

77
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,000
It's antiseptic. Use it.

78
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:02,000
-[Gon gasps]
-[Crazy Slots] What?

79
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,000
Give me a break. Is that it?

80
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:05,000
Come on. Let's go wild, man!

81
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:08,000
Ah, shut up, and go away already.

82
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:12,000
The two of you should leave as well.

83
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Damn it.

84
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Now I'll have to start over
from the beginning.

85
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Well, at least the nest was destroyed.

86
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Damn it, and now
I've got this pointless kill to my credit.

87
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,000
[Gon gasps]

88
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,000
Huh?

89
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Hmm?

90
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:28,000
[dramatic music playing]

91
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Damn it, and now I've got this
pointless kill to my credit.

92
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,000
Hey, are you…

93
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:49,000
Back when I was younger,
are you the one who saved me?

94
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Wait. When?

95
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,000
[Gon] On Whale Island.

96
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:57,000
I'd stumbled onto a foxbear
with her cub in the forest.

97
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,000
-[man] Whale Island?
-[Gon] Remember?

98
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:02,000
You said you had a pointless kill
to your credit because of what I did.

99
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:19,000
Oh, yeah. I remember.

100
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:22,000
I never thought
I'd run into you again here.

101
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:25,000
You sure have grown up, Gon.

102
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,000
-[Killua] Hmm?
-[Gon gasps]

103
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:28,000
But how do you know my name?

104
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
I heard it from your dad, Ging.

105
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,000
[Killua] What?

106
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,000
[Gon] So you know Ging, old man?

107
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:36,000
Old ma--

108
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,000
[sighs]

109
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,000
Yeah, but my name is Kite.

110
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,000
Ging was actually my master.

111
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,000
[both gasp]

112
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:49,000
[serene music playing]

113
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:59,000
[waves crashing]

114
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,000
[creature hisses]

115
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:32,000
Ah, so both of you are
Pro Hunters, too. Is that right?

116
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,000
Yep. Are you one, sir?

117
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,000
Just call me Kite.

118
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:39,000
You're my master's son,
so don't be so formal.

119
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:42,000
Okay. So you're one, too, Kite?

120
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,000
I am.

121
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:47,000
Master Ging's the one who
made me a first-class Hunter.

122
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:50,000
He was my teacher and my benefactor.

123
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:56,000
See, if I had never met Ging,
I'd be dead now,

124
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:59,000
rotting in the back alley
of a slum, probably.

125
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
[man 1] Hey, wait up!

126
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,000
[man 2] Stupid brat!

127
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:31,000
He just stole my bread!

128
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,000
That's all I could find!

129
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
[man 1] Yeah, well, not if we can help it!

130
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,000
[man 2 grunts]

131
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,000
[man 3] Whoa!

132
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Huh?

133
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:03,000
[dog growls]

134
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,000
[man 2] That's my bread!

135
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:10,000
[man 1] You're not getting away
with it this time, punk!

136
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,000
[gasping] Ow!

137
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,000
What the hell is this?

138
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,000
What are you… Stop it!

139
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:20,000
-[dog growling]
-[men gasp]

140
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
[dog barking]

141
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:28,000
[men sigh]

142
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:40,000
[wind blowing]

143
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:51,000
[water dripping]

144
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,000
[footsteps echoing]

145
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:07,000
[light crackling]

146
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,000
[Kite gasps]

147
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,000
[Ging] Uh, hey.

148
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:21,000
So do you live down here with these guys?

149
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,000
It looks fun!

150
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:31,000
[insects chirping]

151
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:35,000
That was it?
That's how you met Ging?

152
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,000
Yeah.

153
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:39,000
Ging told me once

154
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:43,000
that every single Hunter
is well liked by animals.

155
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:47,000
He also told me I had potential,
so that piqued my interest.

156
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:49,000
So you were his student?

157
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,000
Once I forced him to teach me.

158
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:54,000
He's not very fond of anything
that causes him too much hassle,

159
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:58,000
so I was never his student
in any official capacity.

160
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:04,000
But I suppose I can be a little stubborn,
so I just hounded him 'til he caved.

161
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:07,000
A while after that,
I started to develop my Nen,

162
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,000
and he started teaching me to hunt.

163
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:15,000
As a result, I passed the Hunter exam
without much trouble.

164
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:19,000
But Master Ging still wasn't satisfied.

165
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,000
There was another hurdle I had to clear.

166
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Can you guess what that hurdle was?

167
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,000
[Gon] I think I might know.

168
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,000
Yeah?

169
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
[Gon] No. I definitely know.

170
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:41,000
If I know Ging, he probably told you
that he wants you to try and catch him.

171
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:43,000
[Kite chuckles]

172
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Right. That's it exactly.

173
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,000
I knew it!
I thought that was it.

174
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:50,000
But as far as I knew,

175
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:54,000
Ging was the absolute greatest
Hunter in the whole world.

176
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:57,000
It would be the most difficult hunt ever.

177
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,000
There were no clues
or leads to start with.

178
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
Not only that,
there were no rumors of his whereabouts,

179
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:04,000
or sightings of him either.

180
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:09,000
It seemed like he'd managed to
completely erase his existence.

181
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:13,000
[Killua] Like a superpowered
form of Zetsu?

182
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:16,000
And then?
What happened next?

183
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,000
[Kite] I was struggling,

184
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:21,000
grasping for anything
that might help me find him,

185
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:25,000
so I went to his hometown,
to Whale Island.

186
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:30,000
And that was when I first met you, Gon.

187
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,000
[Gon gasps]

188
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:35,000
[Kite] But back then,
I didn't realize you were Ging's son.

189
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,000
I had no idea.

190
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:41,000
I didn't learn that
until I had finally found Ging

191
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:44,000
and told him about what had
happened on Whale Island.

192
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:48,000
[wind blowing]

193
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:55,000
[Ging] That was my kid.
His name's Gon.

194
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,000
[Kite gasps]

195
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,000
[Ging] Thanks for clobbering him.

196
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Some things are just common sense,

197
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:16,000
like avoiding foxbear territory
while they're raising their young. Heh.

198
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,000
[Gon gasps]

199
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:26,000
The fact that I went to Whale Island,
or that I met you there,

200
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,000
none of that seemed to surprise him.

201
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:31,000
It was almost as if he'd expected it.

202
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:35,000
Looking back now,
I think everything that's happened

203
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:37,000
has gone according to Ging's plan.

204
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:40,000
You're saying he set all this up?

205
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Well, I can't prove it.

206
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,000
[Gon] You may be right.

207
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:47,000
Huh?

208
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:51,000
Razor was there waiting for me,

209
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:53,000
Dwun and List, too.

210
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:56,000
Razor and Dwun?

211
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,000
Yeah. It was in a game
called "Greed Island,"

212
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:01,000
but it's kind of a long story.

213
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:05,000
We got inside the game,
and Razor told me he was waiting for me.

214
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:07,000
Ging told him to.

215
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,000
[Ging] One day,
my son's going to come here.

216
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:12,000
When he does, don't hold back.

217
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:15,000
Ha! Fine. Does that mean
that I can kill him?

218
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:19,000
Don't underestimate him.
He is my kid.

219
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:24,000
I'm counting on you. Thanks, Razor.

220
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:29,000
[Gon] Ging created "Greed Island"
with the help of ten of his close friends.

221
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,000
Dwun and List were two of 'em.

222
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Oh! And Razor.
He's also one of Ging's friends.

223
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:40,000
Well, anyway, those three were all there,
just waiting for me.

224
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,000
When I learned that, I realized something.

225
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:45,000
If that was Ging's big plan all along,

226
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,000
for me to go there and meet his friends,

227
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,000
then I wonder if meeting all the others,

228
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:52,000
people like Bisky and everybody else…

229
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:55,000
Well, that might have been
part of his plan, too, right?

230
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,000
[Killua] And if that's really the case,

231
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
then it's also possible
that Ging wanted you

232
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,000
to meet Kite here,
so he helped to make it happen.

233
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,000
[Gon] Think so?

234
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
-Hey, that's right!
-Hmm?

235
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
[Gon] You must have
spent time on Greed Island

236
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,000
at some point, haven't you?

237
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:12,000
[Kite] Me?

238
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:16,000
Yeah. And when you went,
did you register under the name of Nigg?

239
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:21,000
[Kite] Nigg? No, I don't
recall that name. Wait.

240
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:25,000
I do remember Ging taking me
inside a game a while back,

241
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:27,000
now that you mention it.

242
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:28,000
I knew it!

243
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,000
[Kite] "Greed Island."

244
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:33,000
Yes, I believe that's what it was called.

245
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,000
But I can't remember if I used an alias.

246
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:37,000
That's gotta be it!

247
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Ging must have had you register
the name Nigg back then!

248
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Damn it! He got me good! Ohh!

249
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,000
And you were convinced you'd meet him.

250
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:48,000
[Gon groaning in frustration]

251
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:56,000
[Elena] Are you sure
that was the right decision, Ging?

252
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:59,000
[Ging] So, can you make it

253
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:02,000
so that using magnetic force
will send Gon to me,

254
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,000
while using Accompany
will send him to Kite?

255
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:07,000
Yes, I suppose so.

256
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:09,000
But why do you want me to do that?

257
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:12,000
[Ging] If he uses magnetic force
to see me on his own,

258
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:14,000
I guess I'm willing to meet him.

259
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:16,000
But if he's a wimp who needs
to bring his friends along,

260
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:17,000
forget it.

261
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:20,000
Why is he a wimp
if he brings his friends?

262
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:21,000
I don't understand that.

263
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:24,000
[Ging gasps]
Never mind that! Just do it!

264
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,000
More people would just
make you self-conscious, right?

265
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:29,000
Please, just shut up, and do what I asked.

266
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:34,000
Honestly, Ging is so weird.

267
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,000
He's both shy and stubborn.

268
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:39,000
I feel sorry for Gon.

269
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:42,000
[fire crackling]

270
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,000
[Kite] I see.

271
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:46,000
So the real reason
that "Greed Island" was created

272
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:49,000
was to provide you boys
with the type of training you needed.

273
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:52,000
[Killua] No, it was only for Gon, really.

274
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:54,000
I've pretty much been along
for the ride the whole time.

275
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:58,000
But that might have been
part of Ging's plan, too, don't you think?

276
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,000
Even me? Not likely.

277
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:01,000
More like impossible.

278
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:04,000
But it appears
that all of us meeting here

279
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:06,000
was no mere coincidence.

280
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:08,000
[Killua] Yeah. I agree.

281
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:11,000
There's gotta be some
deeper meaning to all this.

282
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,000
Like what?

283
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:16,000
Like Razor waited inside the game
so he could help make you stronger.

284
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:18,000
And if that's the case,
then it would make sense

285
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:20,000
that Ging has some role
for Kite to play, too.

286
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:23,000
A role, huh?

287
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:26,000
You said
that your final test was to find Ging.

288
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,000
-Is that right?
-[Kite] Yeah.

289
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,000
That sounds like a pretty daunting task.

290
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:34,000
The best Hunters in the world
are masters of hunting, sure,

291
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:36,000
but they're also masters
of concealing themselves,

292
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,000
yet you still found him.

293
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:42,000
[Gon] Uh-huh. I think so, too.

294
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:45,000
Once your final test
was completed, Kite,

295
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:46,000
Ging must have made his choice.

296
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,000
You were worthy of handling this.

297
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:51,000
"Handling this"? Wait. What?

298
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:53,000
Oh, come on.

299
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:56,000
Gotta walk you through it?
Basically…

300
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,000
Thanks for clobbering him.

301
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:09,000
[Kite] Hey, Gon.

302
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:10,000
[Gon] Hmm?

303
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:13,000
[Kite] Want me to tell you
where Ging is right now?

304
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:27,000
No, thanks. I'll find him myself.

305
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:30,000
That's a good answer.

306
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,000
So anyway, tell me all about Ging.

307
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:37,000
I wanna hear every story
that you've got about him!

308
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:59,000
[creature chewing]

309
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,000
[Gon] You're kidding me.

310
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,000
How to help two-headed wolves
with breeding?

311
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,000
Ging's really involved in that stuff, too?

312
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,000
[Kite] Of course he is.

313
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:15,000
Ging is involved with a wide
range of Hunter activities.

314
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:17,000
He's never formally applied for it,

315
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:19,000
because he doesn't want
to spend the time or energy,

316
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:22,000
but he's as qualified
as a triple star Hunter.

317
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:24,000
A triple star?

318
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:28,000
Stars are given to Hunters
who perform extraordinary tasks.

319
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:31,000
Those responsible
for historical discoveries,

320
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:34,000
or global achievements
are awarded three stars.

321
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:37,000
There are fewer than ten
of these Hunters in the world.

322
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:41,000
The title "Triple Star Hunter"
is reserved for the very best.

323
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:45,000
Wow. So Ging's as good as
the best Hunters in the world?

324
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:46,000
Awesome!

325
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:56,000
[Killua] So Kite's a Hunter
who's earned Ging's respect.

326
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:01,000
But that isn't all he's done.

327
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:04,000
Ging is also famous
for discovering the Lurka Ruins,

328
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:07,000
not to mention the Kongo Gold Vein.

329
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:08,000
Really? I've heard of that one!

330
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,000
The Lurka Ruins, I mean.

331
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:12,000
[narrator] Kite, Ging's student,

332
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:16,000
his meeting with Gon and Killua
was a clear indication

333
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:19,000
that a brand-new adventure
was about to begin.

334
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:26,000
Meanwhile, on the southern
shores of the Balsa Islands,

335
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:28,000
on the Yorbian Continent,

336
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:31,000
a prologue to an unparalleled fear

337
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:37,000
was steadily,
yet ever so quietly unfolding.

338
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:40,000
[creature] These creatures
simply aren't enough,

339
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,000
no matter how many I eat,

340
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:43,000
but I can't move.

341
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:49,000
I mustn't be hasty.
I must focus on recovering my energy.

342
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:53,000
I must heal
before I can take the next step.

343
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:57,000
[chewing]

344
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:59,000
I have a duty to fulfill.

345
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:03,000
I have to give birth to the King!

346
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:07,000
I am the Queen.

347
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:13,000
[closing theme music playing]

348
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:24,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

349
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:32,000
[dramatic music playing]

350
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:36,000
[inaudible]

351
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:38,000
[Gon] Next time, "Unease and Sighting."

352
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:40,000
Are you uneasy, Killua?

353
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:42,000
[Killua] You're embarrassing me.

354
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:48,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
